{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447366-101-street-level-and-personal-horror-scenarios-warning-dark-subject-matter","id":1447366,"title":"101 Street Level and Personal Horror Scenarios (warning: dark subject matter)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-04T00:53:31-07:00","id":1447366,"title":"101 Street Level and Personal Horror Scenarios (warning: dark subject matter)","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I'm doing another one of my lists. Inspired by my Requiem and Masquerade 5th Edition games, I'm doing a list of dark and gritty storytelling that doesn't require big epic politics or supernatural shenanigans to be entertaining. Really, just stuff that can be resolved quickly but will allow players to get into character. This is going to be a mature thread and involve a lot of dark subject matter but I think people will very much enjoy it. Please contribute if you will.<br /> <br /> I'll be doing a big assembly of the suggestions with proper attribution later on.<br /> <br /> <u>101 Street Level and Personal Horror Scenes</u><br /> <br /> Complete List: <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2021/05/101-street-crime-and-personal-horror.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://unitedfederationofcharles.blo...al-horror.html</a><br /> <br /> 1. The player character finds a man beaten to death in the back of an alley, who will not survive until an ambulance gets there even if one was called now. They have the option of feeding to ease his painful passage, comforting him as he lay dying, or a chance to rob him. If they choose to investigate, they find the mortal responsible nearby who did it because the victim had posted revenge porn about the killer's sister.<br /> <br /> 2. The player characters find an abandoned baby inside a bathroom stall in a vampire night club. The woman's mother was a popular Blood Doll and has ODed nearby. The combination of being fed on and drugs being too much for her. The owner of the club will assure the PCs it will be &quot;taken care of&quot; if they leave the child with his people and dispose of the body. There will always be more where the mother came from.<br /> <br /> 3. The player characters come across an encounter of domestic violence between a couple of their favorite feeding spot regulars that they can choose to intervene in. Both members show signs of injury at the other's hands. Depending on their action, one will kill the other in a few days.<br /> <br /> 4. There is a feral dog that the police are searching for which has killed multiple people. The player characters eventually find it and note that it is a ghoul dog that is guarding a 7 year old Thin Blood with Animalism. She had been killed by her Neonate father and Embraced who then abandoned them in horror. The Prince or Baron will want both the dog and child destroyed as well as their sire tracked down.<br /> <br /> 5. The player characters are approached by a man with a very unusual request. He wants them to kill him in exchange for money for his family. He's in severe medical debt and knows about the undead through his boss. He's a Masquerade breach and figures his blood might be worth something. The Circulatory System actually will offer the PCs $50,000 for him and stiff the family as a suicidal man to tap for years is a great deal no one will question the disappearance of.<br /> <br /> 6. A newly Embraced vampire acquaintance tried feeding on his or her partner and ended up screwing it up, killing them. They call the player characters in hope of help. They are suicidal, close to frenzy, and in a bad state.<br /> <br /> 7. After doing a favor for another vampire, said vampire is sincerely grateful (rare enough) and offers the player characters an unusual gift: there's a pedophile patrolling a nearby area for kids. The vampire says no one will miss em and to have at em.<br /> <br /> 8. The player characters hear gun shots and find a drug deal gone bad with one of the participants dead and the other dying. There's a significant amount of money in both drugs as well as cash available. The murderer on the ground begs to be taken to a hospital despite his botched robbery. An investigation reveals the two men were cousins and both ripping off their employer.<br /> <br /> 9. The player characters are told about a vampire who offed himself via the sunlight and given the keys to his apartment. They're told they can have pretty much anything they want there since this is how Kindred deaths are handled among &quot;friends.&quot; Inside is evidence of a lonely bitter existence culminating in final death.<br /> <br /> 10. See 9# except the player characters also find a child trapped in a special jail cell, two days isolated and dehydrated, as said Kindred was a Ventrue who could only feed on children.<br /> <br /> 11. The player characters find a meat locker full of Dominated and incapacitated human beings just standing around waiting to be tapped for an Elysium meeting. If asked, the &quot;chef&quot; will explain that they're all in debt or agreed to do a drug trial/sleep study they won't remember.<br /> <br /> 12. See 11#, one then wakes up, tries to escape and has no idea how she got here and is freaking out.<br /> <br /> 13. A middle aged ghoul of one Kindred hangout regular is humiliated on a regular basis in disgusting and public ways. If inquired about, they find out he is the Kindred's abusive father. The owner of the local hangout would like the PCs to tell them to leave the guy at home because it's ruining everyone's vibe. Either that or just arrange for the guy to die as a way to help their mental health.<br /> <br /> 14. See 13# but as said ghoul is their Touchstone, killing him actually royally screws them up.<br /> <br /> 15. Speaking of ghoul antics, a man is panicking and begging to do anything for the player characters or other locals. These range from sexual favors to bringing them victims. It's a ghoul that had been cast out by his owner and will who age decades if they don't get a fix soon. Their owner is doing it just to see if the stories about rapid aging are true as he inherited the ghoul as a gift from their sire.<br /> <br /> 16. The player characters are asked to be backup by a vampire who was born in a way that they vaguely allude to as &quot;wrong&quot; but they only have words for in recent decades. They don't want to spend eternity this way and have found someone who can help but doesn't trust them. If the PCs go with them, they find out there is a Neonate Tzimisce doing cosmetic changes to Kindred for blood as well as cash. Is this a trap? Diablerie? Just a job?<br /> <br /> 17. A car crash happens nearby the player characters and it's very likely that people will die in the process. The player characters can play heroes but the spilled blood and possible flames mean that doing so could make it much worse rather than better.<br /> <br /> 18. The player characters come across a violent accident or attack and find themselves unable to look away, transfixed by the sight of the blood as well as violence, for the better part of an hour. This is not natural but they can't get it out of their head.<br /> <br /> 19. The player characters find a teenage boy spraypainting warnings against a particularly upscale house, calling them Monsters and Vampires. The boy is wrong about them being vampires but they are actually containing a serial killer that has been preying on the local minority community for some time. The local Sheriff is planning to make them disappear to discourage the habit of tattling. They are unconcerned about the serial killer.<br /> <br /> 20. A local vagrant screams and is utterly terrified of the player characters, running away, when they see them. They were once successful but in 2004 developed the power to see &quot;Monsters&quot; and it ruined their life, driving them to homelessness as well as madness. Killing them will protect the Masquerade but they have already ignored their calling for decades.<br /> <br /> 21. A vampire with a morality born from comic books and television wants the PCs to help him rescue a bunch of human trafficking victims from the Russian mob. They'll kill or otherwise stop the mobsters, rescue the kidnapees, and turn the latter over to the cops. Things go utterly pear shaped at once when it turns out the cops are helping traffic the victims.<br /> <br /> 22. See #21, if they do succeed then a bunch of vampires buying them will be pissed.<br /> <br /> 23. The player characters are minding their own business when a guy enters their favorite hangout and starts shooting up the place. He is looking for a secret basement where children are being abused. No, there isn't one.<br /> <br /> 24. Humorous as #23 might be from a black comedy perspective, literally thousands of people are checking out his claims on the internet now and it has brought a massive amount of attention online. The PCs need a scapegoat or to shut the place down.<br /> <br /> 25. The PCs hear about a vampire leader in a local community college who is teaching people the mysteries of Caine and Lilith. It is actually a midlife crisis suffering professor using Anne Rice and <i>Fevre Dream </i>to get laid with his Goth Girl students. One of them will commit suicide if he's allowed to continue preying on them due to the humiliation of figuring out it was only a lie. Vampire authorities will find this hilarious rather than sympathetic.<br /> <br /> 26. The player characters meet with a Thin Blood hair stylist who offers to do them well and is quite chatty. The player character then witness the Scourge come in to drag them off to be executed for the crime of being Thin Blood. They'll be stabbed, covered in gasoline, and burned without trial in the parking lot.<br /> <br /> 27. If the PCs take advantage of the 26# stylist, they will find themselves doing odd things and missing time. A Tremere stole all of the hair clippings from the place and used them to do sympathetic magic. This starts small but may escalate to murder.<br /> <br /> 28. A local Blood Doll approaches the PCs and asks them to kill a group of mortals that drugged and abused several of her friends. They are, in every way, complete scum but this is a violation of the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> 29. The player characters find out that they have been made the protagonists of a self-published urban fantasy novel series by a local ghoul who has passed it around to all of her friends. It's harmless and quite terrible but irritating their &quot;scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> 30. It gets less funny in #29 when the ghoul's Toreador or Ministry master beats and want to kill them for making romantic vampire fiction about SOMEONE ELSE<br /> <br /> 31. A police officer believes the PCs are part of a Satanic sex cult or something equally ridiculous. They don't want to bring the PCs in but want to hit the PCs up for bribes and threaten to expose the lot of them.<br /> <br /> 32. The PCs find a wight's den in the bad part of town with something like 50 bodies dragged down there in an enormous pile. No one apparently noticed because no one cared and the thing is still out there killing.<br /> <br /> 33. The world's easiest Blood Hunt concludes when a vampire who mocked a Toreador Elder's art ends up staked then left on the PCs doorstep to be diablerized with a note. Apparently, someone thinks they deserve the opportunity to grow in power. However, killing them or not killing them has consequences and diablerie means they will be a legal &quot;cannibal&quot; with all the social consequences.<br /> <br /> 34. See 33#, the Toreador Elder is actually filming all this because it's a kind of weird morality art as she wants to see what they do.<br /> <br /> 35. A player character feels weird one night and during an altercation with an obnoxious jerk, wakes up hours later with the jerk's body spread all over the walls of a house they don't recognize. Their victim's family is also coming home. What the hell happened!?<br /> <br /> 36. The answer for 35# was that the PCs had drank from a designer drug that is causing a lot of bizarre frenzies. This has caused a half-dozen deaths and the PCs are asked to find whoever is making it and kill the fuck out of them. They're a bunch of college students who have no idea what they've made (possibly with the help of something supernatural).<br /> <br /> 37. The PCs meet a friend from their mortal days who has become entranced with vampire conspiracy theories, harassing club goers, and also recording a podcast about the dark side of their hometown. Mental Disciplines will reveal that he believes in vampires because they are trying to cope with a horrifying but mundane tragedy they're trying to make sense of.<br /> <br /> 38. The PCs get contacted by an acquaintance who is cagey about the problem. When they arrive, the PCs find a little girl who can cause objects to levitate or the walls to bleed. She is both a medium as well as psychic with a Wraith companion. Sadly, there's no school for gifted mutants in this world and she is a danger.<br /> <br /> 39. The PCs find another vampire gloating about how they've been systematically destroying the marriage of a girl or boy they loved in high school. They plan to ghoul them and keep them as a slave (possibly with love having turned to hate). It's as normal to them as chatting about their new Honda. There is absolutely no legal recourse among Kindred.<br /> <br /> 40. A very nervous man is in the local hangout. Talking to them will reveal that he has lost a vampire's entire fortune due to an incredibly stupid Bitcoin investment that turned out to be a scam. They are fully expecting to be murdered by their boss once they arrive, though they aren't 100% sure they're a vampire. They are, however, 100% correct about what is going to happen and see no way out.<br /> <br /> 41. Alternatively for #40, it is not a vampire and they will be killed by a perfectly normal human failed by their accountant. They could also be a ghoul. A baseball bat will be their preferred weapon for beating their former employee to death.<br /> <br /> 42. The PCs are told to investigate rumors of hunters among the city's garbage and fire men of all things. This is true and misleading as a small group of them have created flame throwers and makeshift armor to deal with an infestation of dog-sized cannibal rats that are breeding out of control.<br /> <br /> 43. #42 is just another weird random thing that occasionally happens in the World of Darkness and the PCs are doing the world a favor if they lend them poison gas or whatever to deal with it.<br /> <br /> 44. The local gunsmith the PCs use to stock up on their trench coats and katana offers to sell them silver jacketed bullets or vampire slaying explosive rounds. Even wooden bullets of a low caliber but functional make. The gunsmith doesn't know about the supernatural but knows several of his paranoid nutter customers believe and sees lots of money to be made.<br /> <br /> 45. The PCs have an encounter with the Second Inquisition. Just not the kind of Blade-like encounter they expect. A disgruntled mid-level operative in it wants to sell them information on it because he hates his female boss and co-workers.<br /> <br /> 46. If the PCs do #45, they get contacted by the guy a few days later for killing his wife in a frenzy due to having tried vampire blood he got from either them or another vampire he tried to sell information to. The PCs can use him but only if they cover up his &quot;screw up&quot; and dominate him into a useful pawn.<br /> <br /> 47. The PCs are approached by a former Blood Doll prostitute who wants the PCs to take care of (not necessarily kill) her pimp and make her a ghoul. She'll then take over their business and thinks they can run a vampire food service. While useful as a herd, the number of vessels involved will quickly sicken and die with more than a small number of Kindred feeding on them.<br /> <br /> 48. One of the PC's lovers is hacked and they find themselves on the internet, possibly even so far as a local porn site depending on their feeding habits. This is actually fairly easy to fix and just another disgruntled lover (vampire play is a genre after all) but could get them, the PC, and possibly a dozen other people killed by a panicky Luddite Elder.<br /> <br /> 49. The PCs find themselves dealing with a white middle aged blonde woman with a cellphone that is trying to film them and call the cops on them. If the PCs handle it peacefully, she does it again a few days later and another vampire just snaps her neck out of frustration. It turned out to have been motivated by her catching her child hanging out with these &quot;degenerates.&quot; Now it's an issue.<br /> <br /> 50. The PCs are given an old gas station by a Nosferatu heading out of town. This is a bizarre gift but a free haven is a free haven and the place is still functional. Then the PCs find that the place's basement is utterly stuffed with bodies.<br /> <br /> 51. #50 except the place is actually haunted by an enormously powerful ghost. It is actually capable of possessing people and burning others. The PCs find themselves unable to leave the gas station until they either destroy it or somehow lure their &quot;friend&quot; back to be murdered.<br /> <br /> 52. #50 except the place is now being investigated by the FBI's SAD who are looking into a wildly successful serial killer they believe operated out of the gas station. Ironically, they actually think this is one of their mundane cases as the ratio of human monster to supernatural is still about 3-1.<br /> <br /> 53. The player characters receive a very odd gift in the form of 50 odd years of porn starring a local vampire and sometimes their friends (including a couple of Elders). It takes awhile to realize that not only is this impressive blackmail material, the other vampires weren't always aware they were being filmed.<br /> <br /> 54. A Thin Blood private detective approaches the PCs and says he specializes in odd cases so they don't break the Masquerade. He's in his seventies and not long for this world. Oddly, his request is that the tell a vampire that her mortal father is dying and wants to see her one last time. He can't get close because he messed up with her in the past.<br /> <br /> 55. The vampire gladly accepts if told about #54 and goes to visit their father before the PCs will hear about (or actively witness) her tear their father limb from limb in the most literal way possible. The vampire thanks the PCs and says that they feel much better. Other people may also be caught up in her &quot;therapeutic&quot; frenzy of revenge for their father's past actions.<br /> <br /> 56. A Thin Blooded man or woman wants to offer themselves up as the PCs slave (laborer or sexual) in exchange for protection. They were part of a group before but lost their friends to nastier vampires repeatedly and think they need to work like they're in prison now. It might be E or Lily from <i>Bloodlines</i>.<br /> <br /> 57. If the PCs are stupid enough to agree to #56 without checking, they may find the Thin Blood is actually part of a group planning to diablerize their way into being real Kindred.<br /> <br /> 58. A guy dressed like Duncan Macleod crossed with Blade claims to be a vampire hunter. He is standing around brooding a lot like an idiot but has real weapons. He's not actually a cosplayer or promoting something as everyone assumes but a guy who knows vampires are real. So he's come to &quot;protect&quot; the club scene. He doesn't have the stones to actually attack someone, though.<br /> <br /> 59. A woman is passing out flyers looking for her missing daughter who disappeared a year ago outside the club. She doesn't know vampires exist but it is likely they killed her. The club owner will give free drinks for a month if they make her disappear.<br /> <br /> 60. See #59, the irony is that her daughter is a newly Embraced vampire and now avoiding the club. If she confronts her mother, she'll have an emotional breakdown and reveal everything, which means it's the worst option.<br /> <br /> 61. See #59, another worse irony is her daughter is dead and died horribly in the champagne room. The ghouls just assumed vampires rather than rich mortals did it and cleaned it up as usual.<br /> <br /> 62. The PCs next door neighbors have opened a drug lab and are hosting parties, having shady characters, and drawing needless attention. The PCs can either take over the operation, drive them off, or demand a cut for operating in their territory.<br /> <br /> 63. If the PCs have ready access to Dominate for #62, they also find that they seem strangely immune to it. They're also gross and unappetizing in a way that doesn't make sense. Stray dogs and weird looking homeless people are seemingly checking out the drug lab.<br /> <br /> 64. The Prince or Baron isn't fond of &quot;degenerates&quot; (there's that word again) and upon discovery that their private server for the &quot;Bitcoin thing&quot; (that too?) is being used to traffic in particularly monstrous forms of pornography, probably snuff, asks the PCs to go kill the man running it along with finding a replacement for managing the &quot;normal&quot; part of the business. They can do it themselves if they want, possibly cheating them of vast money.<br /> <br /> 65. The manager in #64 actually tries to save his life by saying he has all their addresses and identities. It could be a lot of guilt-free eating but is mass murder really the solution here? Is it not?<br /> <br /> 66. Certainly the studios for #65 is a place where Humanity loss would be very minor if they killed everyone present.<br /> <br /> 67. The Assistant District Attorney tries to get the PCs to testify against another vampire's mortal identity, threatening them and pleading on their consciences for whatever horrible thing her target is doing. The other vampires find this hilarious and are already taking bets on how they will be horribly humiliated, discredited, enslaved, or killed.<br /> <br /> 68. The PCs find someone, a friend of theirs, to try to get the ADA of #67 to back off before it is their head. Apparently, they were sent on this as a suicide mission from the Mayor or DA because they turned down participation in an illegal venture (or sexual favors--this is a sleazy sleazy world).<br /> <br /> 69. A Ventrue is so pleased with the PCs that he invites them to participate in a business venture. Some investigating will reveal that it is a Ponzi scheme or a Pump and Dump about to collapse. The Ventrue believes with the PCs help, they can keep it going for a few more years and make massive gains before disappearing with the loot.<br /> <br /> 70. The Ventrue in #69 actually plans to frame them for its collapse because his biggest customers are Elders who he pretended to be a genius for and needs someone to blame for the fact he's run out of money.<br /> <br /> 71. The Ventrue in #69 is entirely sincere but the lives he's ruined as a financial parasite are far greater in number than he's ever done as a literal blood-drinking one.<br /> <br /> 72. A spectacularly bigoted cop has been framing black men and gay men for the murders committed by Kindred since he joined the force thirty years ago. He's now retiring and expects to be rewarded with the Embrace. The PCs are asked to take him out to the fields and &quot;Old Yeller&quot; him.<br /> <br /> 73. See 72#, but the cop saw this coming and claims he has plenty of evidence if they don't Embrace him. The Prince will actually grant permission for it if they call him because he considers it initiative. The cop will be as monstrous a Hound as he was a cop, though.<br /> <br /> 74. The PCs are approached by an old billionaire on blood thinners who wants the Embrace. He'll give them the equivalent of Resources 5 if they do it (maybe 10-20 million plus a mansion depending on how the PCs bargain). He has ties to the Second Inquisition and plans to use them to eliminate rivals and set himself up as a power in their city. He controls two US Senators and already has a Low Humanity score.<br /> <br /> 75. See 74#, he's actually not a billionaire at all. He's squatting in a mansion up for sale after its real owner's death and the people he's hired as security are just local actors. He fully intends to stiff the PCs with the bill.<br /> <br /> 76. See #75 and he is a former ghoul allowed to age to 90 after spending most of his life as a 20 year old. His old master will not be pleased that his ex-employee is now immortal and has access to all of his secrets.<br /> <br /> 77. A well-meaning vampire (they exist, sometimes) tried to treat the patients of his hospital job by giving them bits of vampire blood to help in their recoveries. While this helped with some, it actually resulted in a lot of them becoming violent and dangerous to their families. The Sheriff wants the guy staked and held up to the sunlight. They can be bargained into clemency if the vampire is forced to make restitution in some awful way like helping bleed patients.<br /> <br /> 78. The PCs are given a very valuable painting by an associate. It was stolen from a Toreador Elder a long time ago and they have since met the Final Death. Their childer will be very pissed at not possessing it as they were both artiste and (nude) model for it respectively. It's all fun and games until they start threatening horrible revenge or death against each other's servants.<br /> <br /> 79. The PCs are asked to give a ride to a Nosferatu to a motel in the middle of nowhere because the vampire doesn't have a car. While waiting, the building blows up and a massive gun fight breaks out that the PCs may be caught up in. The Nosferatu coming back with two massive bags of cash. The Nosferatu will cut them in but refuse to explain what the fuck just happened.<br /> <br /> 80. See 79# but add a car chase and later ninjas.<br /> <br /> 81. People dying due to Covid-19 in a particularly nasty outbreak. It's due to a Thin Blood with a mouth deformity that spreads the infected blood rapidly as well as increases its potency. Every vampire in the city wants them dead and is ready to kill all Thin Bloods and Caitiff in the city over this.<br /> <br /> 82. See 81#, it actually is just a rumor started by a Malkavian and there's no such thing as a plague-bearing Thin Blood. The people just died of the disease regularly and its hysteria in action.<br /> <br /> 83. Several members of a venerated Old Money family have been murdered or died in suspicious accidents. This is pretty Masquerade breaking, especially as there's a Ventrue in the city of said family. Someone is clearly planning to remove the bloodline and drive him to torpor.<br /> <br /> 84. See 83#. The Ventrue actually feeds on domestic servants and is killing his bloodline so he can liquidate the family assets since he was recently ruined. He plans to kill another ten or so people then blame it on &quot;cartels or something.&quot;<br /> <br /> 85. Elizabeth Bathory was not a vampire but one of her self-stylized spiritual successors has been kidnapping young minority women to do blood baths. The PCs are asked to investigate but already the locals are forming an old fashioned lynch mob to go after her and anyone she was seen with on social media.<br /> <br /> 86. See 85#, the irony being that she actually is in her mansion as a wight since bathing in the blood caused her to frenzy and go insane until she lost everything remaining of what she was.<br /> <br /> 87. A predatory loan business has moved into a neighborhood and people are disappearing left and right. They're planning to gentrify the neighborhood and are going to replace everything with stories that sell nothing. The PCs can either try to profit off of this or shut it down, depending on how they like the neighborhood.<br /> <br /> 88. There's an actual slaving ring that provides Kindred with young men or women to purchase, Blood Bond, and brainwash before they pick up their property. Either that or just have them sent as meals. It is handled via an app and some tech savvy youngsters who think they're geniuses for this. It is not nearly as innovative as they think but not illegal either. What the PCs do about it is up to them.<br /> <br /> 89. A witness in the Witness Protection Program was a member of a local vampire's gang. Their former boss would like them to be taken care of. If the PCs aren't up for murder for hire, point out that they know too much and erasing their memories of vampiredom is also a good idea.<br /> <br /> 90. This is 89#, a trap by the Second Inquisition. Their bait is terrified that he's being set up and 100% correct about their expendability.<br /> <br /> 91. The PCs wake up in a tub with a missing organ or two. A Kindred prankster told where their &quot;newly dead&quot; bodies were and it was transported by organ leggers to transport (thankfully in a sunlight proof body bag). The PCs are probably very irritated.<br /> <br /> 92. The PCs are asked to get a pair of children out of town. This is because their parents were recently killed by the Prince and the Sheriff couldn't go through with the order to kill them too.<br /> <br /> 93. See 91#. The thing is the children are dhampyr already drinking blood and are hopeless psychopaths. Possibly even Revenants.<br /> <br /> 94. A man is bothering a woman at the PC's hang out, insisting they're his wife and that they have a child together. She eventually calls the cops on him. Later, a vampire admits the guy pissed him off so he used Dominate to erase all her memories of the guy and implant new ones that he's a stalker. He's wondering how long it will last until their brains break.<br /> <br /> 95. For 94#. He actually implanted the memory of their marriage and fatherhood into his brain. Dude is a dick.<br /> <br /> 96. A prostitute shows up to the PCs home and says they were paid for by a friend. Their blood is laced with a chemical harmless to humans but incapacitating to vampires, possibly magical in origin. It is a very bizarre Hunter.<br /> <br /> 97. A group of human vigilantes are going to go and slaughter a camp of homeless individuals squatting in an abandoned building. This is because an investor wants to redevelop the land. The group is only supposed to drive them out but the police could give two shits about whatever happens there. The PCs can involve themselves or ignore it.<br /> <br /> 98. A mobile clinic is providing free healthcare to the homeless but they're getting extremely sick as a result. Some have even died. Is a Kindred using it to feed on the least fortunate? Is it medical experimentation? Pentex? Technocrats? No, it's actually the fact that its a local teaching college's project and they're using a lot of expired products with incompetent students.<br /> <br /> 99. There's a farm full of guys who are kidnapping travelers, killing them, and feeding them to pigs. Nothing supernatural, just a bunch of sickos. An associate of theres thinks that they could be turned into a useful service for Kindred.<br /> <br /> 100. The player characters find a van full of guns, explosives, and about $30,000 in drugs as well as cash. Someone is either dead or a complete moron.<br /> <br /> 101. The player characters are inside a grocery store getting orange juice, paper towels, cookies, duct tape, plastic wrap, color safe bleach, and a few other things you need as a vampire. That's when a group of violent drug addicted criminals come in to rob the place and handle it in the most unprofessional manner possible, possibly taking them hostage or killing customers. The police may actually show up soon because this is their second robbery of the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-08-2021, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T03:17:14-07:00","id":1447381,"title":"","content":"&quot;24. Humorous as #23 might be from a black comedy perspective, literally thousands of people are checking out his claims on the internet now and it has brought a massive amount of attention online. The PCs need a scapegoat or to shut the place down.&quot;<br /> <br /> Actually we had excactly this in our Mage round once and to make it even better it whas from a new ST that came from VtM because our ST wanted to play for some time and the ST where surprised because he actually solved our problems because we had just planed from last session how can uncover a child traffic ring without to much suspission.<br /> <br /> 102. An Ancilla that is somewhat famous in the local szene is following a little child for some time now. Suddenly there is an uproar in the scene where the ancilla is suspected to be a pedophile wanting his next victim. After talking it is turned out the child is his grandchild and he watches it since the mother that whas his daughter died. Because the Ancilla is to important but not wanting to stop is the local prince want for solving the problem, that the pcs are kidnapping the child and put it in some cellar of a pedophile or serial killer for a scapegoat and the Ancilla stop this.<br /> <br /> 103. like 102. but the (step)father of the child abuses it and the ancilla tried to take it to him for taking care before all this happened.<br /> <br /> 104. like 102. but the uproar where arranged by a Niktuku that want the child for embrace and so get the Ancilla out of the way.<br /> <br /> 105. the single mother that the PCs are friends with is lamentating about how her child is now acting strange. After finding it, it turn out it become awake as a Dhampire so the one night stand of the mother whas a thinblood<br /> <br /> 106. like 105. but the mother is actually knowing all the time about the whole masquerade thing where you now need to ask, why and that if the Sheriff find out about her son you need to take care of her too.<br /> <br /> 107. like 106. but she knows it because she whas all the time an undercover SI agent that is trying to find out who are just cursed corpses and who are the real monsters that need to hunt down.<br /> <br /> 108. A local tremere that is in love with a mortal is somehow on the target list of the SI and begs the Players to help him/her escape together with the spouse.<br /> <br /> 109. like 109. but the spouse is a Mage that would offer the players for their help per day one bathtube full of blood. Of course the players are free to reject the offer and making them get into the SI crossfire but do they want to offend a mage?<br /> <br /> 110. like 109. but the spouse is in reality an SI agent that is unboundable","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-04-2021, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T03:33:25-07:00","id":1447383,"title":"","content":"Oooo, some really good ones there!<br /> <br /> I like the whole idea of a Kindred stalking their family for good reasons due to their being a much worse predator about but potentially making things worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T06:23:25-07:00","id":1447393,"title":"","content":"- An influentual character, perhaps the prince, invites the players to hunt with him, as a social activity. You travel to his secluded domain where he offers hunting items (Ghouled horses, dogs, weapons). He then releases a mortal, gives the mortal a headstart, and the players can give chase.<br /> Variant 1- The character lets the players win, only the subject of the hunt was important to another vampire, and the players are going to earn their ire. For bonus blame, have the players select their quarry; their choice will dictate who they offend. The other would-be victims are returned to their masters (to tell the tale) <br /> Variant 2- The vampire allows the players a good chase, but ultimately swoops in at the last moment to take the kill, making sure to utterly destroy the victim as part of a power-play to intimidate the players; this could be them. <br /> <br /> -A vampire died, and his things, including his ghouls, are being auctioned off by the prince. If nobody bids, the ghouls will be slaughtered (or perhaps hunted as above) <br /> <br /> -The players discover a vampire's project to breed a revenant family. There are bodies of failures/thinbloods (and failed thinbloods), about half a dozen pregnant women eager to have the first revenant in order to please the master, terrible living conditions, failed ritual areas, and all the budget-horror doctor apparatuses you can find. <br /> <br /> -You're in dire straits and you're desperate for blood. A vampire offers you access to her herd. She takes you into her dungeon to make your choice. Cue whatever the fuck is the sweet spot of horrifying but not triggering (kids? Tortured men? Pretty women with their faces scratched off? An ethnic group?) The Vampire is completely oblivious to any notion of wrongdoing, honestly rather impressed with herself. She'll probably drive herself into frenzy if the players question her. <br /> <br /> -You meet a Cleaver, who appears to be around 30, Husband, also 30ish , two kids; one eight and the other three. one dog. All seems fine, everyone loves mother, but there's a picture on the fridge; Same family, same ages. 1987.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T06:38:04-07:00","id":1447395,"title":"","content":"The Cleaver one is especially nasty. Good job!<br /> <br /> Also, nice job adapting the nuts and bolts of trying to make a Revenant Family being pretty damn horrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T06:51:23-07:00","id":1447398,"title":"","content":"-Your dog(s) have been taken by someone, you're guided into learning that the dog(s) eventually went to a Tzmisce who has half scrambled them as research materials in an effort to learn a particular procedure. Perhaps the Tzmisce did this as a power move, or perhaps someone set this up to set you against the Tzmisce, or perhaps it's an honest mistake. Perhaps the Tzmisce will attempt to un-scramble the dog in apology if you approach diplomatically, but the dog, imperfectly corrected and traumatized, will never be the same. Your dog was not the only victim, there's a considerable bodypile waiting incineration in the Tzmisce's haven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T06:55:17-07:00","id":1447399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447366-101-street-level-and-personal-horror-scenarios-warning-dark-subject-matter?p=1447398#post1447398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Your dog(s) have been taken by someone, you're guided into learning that the dog(s) eventually went to a Tzmisce who has half scrambled them as research materials in an effort to learn a particular procedure. Perhaps the Tzmisce did this as a power move, or perhaps someone set this up to set you against the Tzmisce, or perhaps it's an honest mistake. Perhaps the Tzmisce will attempt to un-scramble the dog in apology if you approach diplomatically, but the dog, imperfectly corrected and traumatized, will never be the same. Your dog was not the only victim, there's a considerable bodypile waiting incineration in the Tzmisce's haven.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the dog's owner was named John Wick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T03:23:38-07:00","id":1447555,"title":"","content":"For me, the big trick to doing Street Level and Personal Horror <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> is to draw from sources other than vampire fiction. I think gangster movies are a very good source of these sort of things and having things like issues over money, revenge, personal issues, and the violence among regular people gives great opportunities for vampire characters. Their powers allow them to deal with already interesting situations that don't need huge amounts of the supernatural to be interesting. The supernatural is more of a spice.<br /> <br /> I also think that its important to not get too glamorous with your PCs. One thing I liked about Bloodlines is the fact that the first haven is really the best haven. It's a terrible place in the ratty part of town but you are surrounded by meals. Giving a sense that the PC has to keep an eye out for money, better lodgings, and their next meal (whether they grab them off the street or not) makes the game feel more desperate.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://lparchive.org/Vampire-The-Masquerade-Bloodlines-(by-gatz-and-TheMcD)/Update%2004/2-ibRunt0ZR7ucK.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I think doing the Bioware thing and making large amounts of moral choices available is also another way of doing personal horror. It doesn't have to be choices of two terrible decisions but making it a little ambiguous certainly helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T14:28:13-07:00","id":1447631,"title":"","content":"\u201c<br /> 21. A vampire with a morality born from comic books and television wants the PCs to help him rescue a bunch of human trafficking victims from the Russian mob. They'll kill or otherwise stop the mobsters, rescue the kidnapees, and turn the latter over to the cops. Things go utterly pear shaped at once when it turns out the cops are helping traffic the victims.\u201d<br /> <br /> Why wouldn\u2019t a bunch of Vampires in the World of Darkness wouldn\u2019t assume cops are corrupt?<br /> <br /> Also I have another one form a story I plan on doing.<br /> <br /> One of the PCs sires have issues with their Childer or another older vampire if the PCs sire is not applicable.<br /> <br /> You get a call as it turns out they discovered a mortal their attached to AKA Touchstone and has conditioned them with Dominate and presence. They then gently suggest some unpleasant favors for your cotiaere to do and that their touchstone will be fine if they stay in their good graces. And","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T20:06:36-07:00","id":1447687,"title":"","content":"I am borrowing #11, #12, and #101 for the MtAs game I am planning - vampires are going to be among the villains of the campaign.<br /> <br /> #112. A powerful and important vampire asks a PC vampire (one with corporate connections or hacking ability or something similar) to help in canceling the life insurance of mortals targeted for death by the Camarilla. This is done purely out of spite. But the vampire who makes the request will owe a boon to the PCs who helps.<br /> <br /> #113. A powerful and important vampire tasks the coterie with destroying a clinic which helps people recover from addiction, a shelter for battered women, or something similar. A Ventrue feeds on these social victims and decent people helping those victims complicates the feeding. The vampire who makes the request will owe a boon to the PCs who help.<br /> <br /> #114 The coterie learns of an ananke Malkavian (fortune telling through organ reading) vampire who selects victims through dating apps, and typically targets lonely men. The Malkavian is in the court of the prince, much respected, and liked by the powers that be. A mortal friend, possibly a touchstone, who knows the party tells them about his forthcoming blind date, which the coterie realizes is with the ananke Malkavian. It will help the coteries social standing if they do not disturb the ananke and the way it operates. They will face real trouble if they interfere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T20:10:02-07:00","id":1447688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447366-101-street-level-and-personal-horror-scenarios-warning-dark-subject-matter?p=1447399#post1447399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the dog's owner was named John Wick.</div> </div> </div> </div>That poor vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T21:09:03-07:00","id":1447691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447366-101-street-level-and-personal-horror-scenarios-warning-dark-subject-matter?p=1447631#post1447631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cWhy wouldn\u2019t a bunch of Vampires in the World of Darkness wouldn\u2019t assume cops are corrupt?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that they think the cops would look the other way but now with them involved, the vampires have to kill a bunch of cops potentially now too and find a new way of getting the victims to safety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the PCs sires have issues with their Childer or another older vampire if the PCs sire is not applicable.<br /> <br /> You get a call as it turns out they discovered a mortal their attached to AKA Touchstone and has conditioned them with Dominate and presence. They then gently suggest some unpleasant favors for your cotiaere to do and that their touchstone will be fine if they stay in their good graces. And </div> </div> </div>Oooo, that's a good one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447366-101-street-level-and-personal-horror-scenarios-warning-dark-subject-matter?p=1447687#post1447687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am borrowing #11, #12, and #101 for the MtAs game I am planning - vampires are going to be among the villains of the campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! That's great news. Glad I could contribute a little to your campaign.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> #112. A powerful and important vampire asks a PC vampire (one with corporate connections or hacking ability or something similar) to help in canceling the life insurance of mortals targeted for death by the Camarilla. This is done purely out of spite. But the vampire who makes the request will owe a boon to the PCs who helps.<br /> <br /> #113. A powerful and important vampire tasks the coterie with destroying a clinic which helps people recover from addiction, a shelter for battered women, or something similar. A Ventrue feeds on these social victims and decent people helping those victims complicates the feeding. The vampire who makes the request will owe a boon to the PCs who help.<br /> <br /> #114 The coterie learns of an ananke Malkavian (fortune telling through organ reading) vampire who selects victims through dating apps, and typically targets lonely men. The Malkavian is in the court of the prince, much respected, and liked by the powers that be. A mortal friend, possibly a touchstone, who knows the party tells them about his forthcoming blind date, which the coterie realizes is with the ananke Malkavian. It will help the coteries social standing if they do not disturb the ananke and the way it operates. They will face real trouble if they interfere. </div> </div> </div>Nicely dark and appropriate for street level campaigns.<br /> <br /> The only thing necessary for evil to triumph is good men to do nothing but vampires aren't ever good are they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T13:16:15-07:00","id":1447971,"title":"","content":"Jumpin' Absimiliard on a pogo stick, there are so <i>many </i>inspiring ideas here. Would you mind if I adapted some of them as seed-plots to the generator I discuss in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444474-v20-vampire-the-masquerade-20th-anniversary-setting-generator\">this thread</a>? My inspiration is hitting a wall in that department at the moment, but many of these ideas would really add variety to the results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T13:20:00-07:00","id":1447974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr. Gerald Ravenpie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447366-101-street-level-and-personal-horror-scenarios-warning-dark-subject-matter?p=1447971#post1447971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jumpin' Absimiliard on a pogo stick, there are so <i>many </i>inspiring ideas here. Would you mind if I adapted some of them as seed-plots to the generator I discuss in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444474-v20-vampire-the-masquerade-20th-anniversary-setting-generator\">this thread</a>? My inspiration is hitting a wall in that department at the moment, but many of these ideas would really add variety to the results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, absolutely, go ahead.<br /> <br /> I created it because I realized so many of my ideas and inspirations were fantasy or action orientated. There didn't seem to many rules or ideas on how to do street level or gritty gaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T13:47:48-07:00","id":1447980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447366-101-street-level-and-personal-horror-scenarios-warning-dark-subject-matter?p=1447974#post1447974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, absolutely, go ahead.<br /> <br /> I created it because I realized so many of my ideas and inspirations were fantasy or action orientated. There didn't seem to many rules or ideas on how to do street level or gritty gaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Quite a number of these stories hit the &quot;<i>interesting rumors that are being talked about in the city these nights</i>&quot; nail in the head. I was in need of precisely stories like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26787-dr-gerald-ravenpie","name":"Dr. Gerald Ravenpie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26787_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T06:02:27-07:00","id":1448317,"title":"","content":"There's a Vampire film <i>The Hunger</i> (1983), and it provides a drastic example of what happens when (major spoiler) <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> A very old Ghoul is denied Vitae, in VtM terms/interpretation. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> I recommend this film to every VtM fan! It's nice to see the Ankh being used in Vampire fiction predating VtM. (Does anyone know when and how this symbol got associated with Vampires?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-12-2021, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T09:21:10-07:00","id":1448429,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d guess probably back in the 70s or 80s. The ankh was really popular in goth circles and showed up in a lot of iconography and jewelry; because it meant \u2018life\u2019, and was Egyptian, and looked cool. Plus Egypt gets tied into vampires with Anne Rice\u2019s books and some pretty important Egyptian plot points so I imagine it\u2019s some combination of Queen of the Damned and Sandman and just the Ankh being really cool looking, popular with goths, and interestingly ironic for vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T18:24:27-07:00","id":1448736,"title":"","content":"#115: A Tremere attempts to rope some of the PCs into helping him dispose of some issues with his work at a women's health clinic. He is performing experiments involving abortions, and needs help with covering up deaths, disappearances, and funding. He will offer a minor boon for this help.<br /> <br /> #116: Some Nosferatu tasks the PCs with killing a human faith healer. The faith healer can perform real miracles apparently, and it would be bad for the human cattle to believe in miracles. Also, she embarrassed the elder when he came to try and get her to fix his face. He will offer a minor boon for this help.<br /> <br /> #117: A Toreador, with a strong position in the local Camarilla, murders mortal artists after they have produced a work that places them on the cultural map. The Toreador's thinking is this prevents the artists from disappointing people with future mediocrity and the murder gives the work a lovely patina tragedy. The Toreador asks for PCs help with such a murder. He will offer a minor boon for this help.<br /> <br /> #118: Someone - such as reporter, a law officer, worried parent, etc - is investigating a clinic for youths with substances abuse issues. A Malkavian is using the clinic as part of human smuggling. He tasks the PCs to do something about the investigation. He will offer a minor boon for this help.<br /> <br /> #119: A new business, and local success story, is doing well and forcing a Ventrue owned and run business to actually compete in the local market place. A Ventrue tasks the PCs with kidnapping an owner so the Ventrue can lock them in a cage for a week or so and blood bond them (that's how this Ventrue rolls). He will offer a minor boon for this help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T19:02:35-07:00","id":1448740,"title":"","content":"Very nice ones! I especially like 116.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T19:30:25-07:00","id":1449078,"title":"","content":"120)<br /> &quot;<i>Her sweet unbeating heart, her beautiful pallor, her lovely fangs...</i>&quot;<br /> Such have lately been the thoughts, feelings, and attitude of a Ghoul belonging to a local Neonate. Some would comment that perhaps he has been a hopeless romantic all along; while others would point out that this is simply a peculiar manifestation of the Blood Bond. The truth is that a pair of Toreador Ancillae - a woman and a man - have revealed themselves to the Ghoul (after double-checking that he is one of the Ghouls who is aware of Vampires) and took him under a sort of mentorship. Through heartfelt anecdotes, tearful confessions, passionate ruminations, and judicious use of Presence the pair of Toreadors has convinced the Ghoul that he can serve and please his mistress in much more...intimate...ways that he hasn't considered before. All that was needed was a bit of soul-searching, and with the (seemingly) earnest help of the pair of Ancillae the Ghoul's passions have indeed become profoundly aligned to the ideal of unique and exceptional vampiric beauty.<br /> <br /> The Ghoul is ready and willing to assume the role of a cherished companion. In what little free time he has he took up running to get into shape. He has also bought blood on the side from a blood bank, to surprise his mistress with a gift. His Ancillae benefactors have warned him about the possibility of rejection and punishment, but even they - in all their toreador matchmaking wisdom - do not have a full picture of what might happen.<br /> <br /> Whether it will be when he will pour a glass of blood for her out of a champagne bottle, or after he complements her fangs, or as he strips naked to offer his body, his mistress might get a hint. Once the Ghoul confesses his feelings and ambitions to the beautiful Vampire woman, and will offer to satisfy her in any way, she might have three realizations. First - her servant has fetishized her being undead, without her prior approval. Second - without her permission he dared to assume that he might be cherished as a lover by her. Third - all that the first two gave him is that he became desperately needy, clingy, annoying, and cloying. One, even two, of these might have resulted in a harsh but fair punishment. But all three together might just be too much according to the alluring Neonate, as she is demanding and prideful.<br /> She won't abandon him, of course not. This man is a loyal servant after all. But it is very likely that the romantic Ghoul will end up not only with a broken heart, but with many broken bones. Especially if he reveals in the end that he agreed to relationship advice given by the pair of Toreadors.<br /> <br /> Can the PCs help this Ghoul before his mistress scourges him? Or maybe they will take upon themselves the task of punishing the Ghoul? Can the pair of Toreador Ancillae be reached? And just what is their angle for doing this, other than dilettante curiosity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-20-2021, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T07:39:55-07:00","id":1449189,"title":"","content":"121: More of a black humor occasion, but still works for a minor issue that needs solving and could lead to genuine horror and dark moments.<br /> <br /> There's some kind of scene, a group. It's about comics or a bookclub or an actual academics meeting, whatever. The point is that it's a gathering for a some very passionate people with some very firm Opinions<sup>TM</sup> about the subject matter, and any meeting is liable to turn into an argument.<br /> Then kindred get involved - specifically Toreador and/or Brujah - who also have very firm Opinions<sup>TM</sup>, to the point where it'll build their tempers up a hairsbreadth away from the beast making their point for them. The meeting is now liable to turn into a massacre, a masquerade violation, or at least a murder. The Brujah don't deal well with opposing viewpoints. Toreador can get dangerously petty if you offend their taste and artistic/academic qualifications, and may hire the coterie to help humiliate an offender in a vicious fashion. Maybe it's their art being criticised. The group is just regular people with a passion for their hobbies, but a vampire has decided they have the wrong opinions about something harmless and so must die or worse, apparently.<br /> <br /> Possibly the coterie is passing by and one of the party can't help getting drawn in, and they're the one who gets offended.<br /> <br /> (Everybody thinks the Toreador are soft and less animalistic until you walk into one of their monthly bookclub meetings. Somebody is arguing about the historic context for something, while the opposing viewpoint in the back, frothing bloody foam at the mouth, howls &quot;I. Was. <i>Literally. </i>There. You. <i>Hack</i>!!!&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-21-2021, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T12:17:51-07:00","id":1450864,"title":"","content":"122)<br /> <br /> The player characters are approached by a Ghoul of a Malkavian Elder and given a thin (32 pages) notebook. It is filled with dense handwriting with rows upon rows of short descriptions of mortals. &quot;<i>Young working class with a beautiful wife, and at least one child</i>&quot;, &quot;<i>Middle-aged lonely businessman or lawyer</i>&quot;, &quot;S<i>hort and thin, dwelling near the city center</i>&quot;, &quot;<i>A clown or another circus performer with many friends</i>&quot; and so on.<br /> The Ghoul explains that his lord requires mortals to possess with his formidable Dominate powers, and requests help in finding and acquiring them. It is not just about the bodies, the physical qualities - the Elder is also interested in what sort of existence these mortals have, so that he can experience new circumstances and interact with a variety of persons. The Ghoul elaborates that the PCs' job would be just to find the mortals and lead them to an agreed-upon isolated place - a parking lot on the city's outskirts, an isolated dark alley, an abandoned office building, and similar. From there they will be kidnapped into a vehicle by a team of Ghouls led by the Elder's Grandchilde, who of course will use his mental powers to subdue the acquisition.<br /> <br /> The Malkavian Elder promises tangible rewards if the PCs bring him many mortals to overtake. It is their choice whether it will be pull within mortal institutions, information in regard to Kindred society and their goings-on, or simply cash given for the time and effort. Or some other agreed-upon method of recompense. Perhaps even a minor Boon, though only if enough particularly interesting mortals are found and acquired.<br /> The Ghoul messenger assures there little to no risk involved. The actual kidnapping is done by the Grandchilde and the Ghouls. After the Elder fulfills his intentions, a mortal's memories of the whole occurrence will be removed or altered, and he will be put back on the streets without further ado. And the Ghoul's lord has principles - no women or children will be singled out for possession. Finally, the Ghoul notes that the work of finding the mortals can be quite interesting. Certainly, there is a lot of variety to encounter, and the Elder provides freedom of choice as to who to kidnap from within the described mortals. Though sometimes in a notebook there are written indicators of priority.<br /> <br /> The proposed work seems straightforward and rather easy. Beyond the promised tangible rewards, there is also the fact that the very act of cooperating with an Elder might bring future benefits beyond the outlined ones.<br /> However, what if the Malkavian uses Possession to further his schemes, pranks, and plots in regard to other Vampires? If the PCs help him, they might be held responsible for events and outcomes they knew nothing about. And there is also the possibility of the PCs losing themselves in the undertaking - after all, there are hundreds of thousands of mortals in the city. And it just seems certain the Malkavian Elder can and will regularly fill another thin notebook with rows of tiny, laconic descriptions of wanted mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-04-2021, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T15:54:39-07:00","id":1451263,"title":"","content":"123)<br /> <br /> A trio of Malkavian Ancillae - two men and one woman - have become fans of the Joker from Batman comics after watching the newest <i>Joker </i>with Joaquin Phoenix. Fascinated with the deadly criminal clown, they watched all the Batman movies featuring the fictional character, and browsed through some comics. Get enough Malkavians in one place, and they come up with very surprising ideas and plots. Through intense and intricate psychological conditioning (including the use of Disciplines) they want to create their own Joker, a Ghoul who will become an amalgam of the various takes on the character. They will work on him to such an extent that he will even be uncertain exactly how, why, and when he became the Joker; mimicking the mysterious past of the character in the media.<br /> He will be their elite, stylish errand boy and enforcer, though the Joker will also be given some freedom to express and develop his newly instilled tendencies. And there will be no Batman, nor a commissioner Gordon to stop him.<br /> <br /> The Joker would be provided with weapons, information, funds, thugs, and safehouses by his shadowy benefactors. The Malkavian Vampires are so pleased with their idea that their attitude is along the lines of - &quot;Just how cool is that?&quot;. Certainly most Vampires - and their Ghouls - in the city will never be prepared for someone like him. The weak will be confused and terrified, while the strong will be impressed. There will be more to him than just violence - he will of course have a sharp sense of humor, and a kind of rugged wisdom and insight. Though the Malkavians just cannot agree on what kind of look to go with for the Joker, but surely with time, they will reach a consensus that will result in a very distinctive appearance. And if the Joker gets killed or captured, then they can make a new one - so the Joker will be returning, just like in the comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-15-2021, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T04:39:20-07:00","id":1457258,"title":"","content":"124)<br /> <br /> A Nosferatu Ancillae approaches the player characters and tells them about a curious new visitor at the Elysium. Apparently, it is a Tremere Vampire, but not the kind of they might be used to. He promises that what she will propose and offer might either greatly interest or greatly amuse them.<br /> <br /> And fair enough, there is a very attractive and nicely dressed female Tremere Vampire in the Elysium, and she approaches the PCs and introduces herself as a Carnian Vampire, belonging to House Carna under the leadership of Carna. She informs them that she is currently seeking a mortal men who could potentially be a new lover for Carna, and she requires aid in finding and securing such a man. Like a litany, she recites the requirements for such a man.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cMust of course understand how to worship and appreciate the woman he loves, and definitely should love magic for the sake of it. Must be caring, insightful, and obedient. All in all, the man should know his place, and must care about the relation of course! Never speak up. Ideally, he would enjoy nature and the great outdoors, and walks during beautiful nights. And for finding such a man, such a potential lover for the esteemed Carna, she and I offer to you the Friendship of House Carna. I am sure it will bring you great joy and many benefits, if you will only earn it with this simple, but profound and meaningful, help given to Carna.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The PCs can inquire the Carnian Vampire about the specifics of the arrangement in regard to this potential lover and what is intended for him, but the Tremere Vampire will be politely secretive about this. She will however give information about the task of finding the man. It turns out that the man does not need to have all the qualities described initially \u2013 but at least over half of them should be present. It is also valid to inspire such qualities in a potential lover for Carna, to guide him in this. If asked about what Friendship of House Carna entails, the Tremere Vampire will smile nicely and just say that it is built on mutual trust and loyalty, and that it can indeed be truly wonderful for those involved.<br /> <br /> If the PCs heard rumors that Carna has harmed her lovers in the past, the Tremere Vampire will vehemently deny this, saying <i>\u201cNone of this happened! In fact, all lovers of Carna simply left her\u2026men are so uncertain in their feelings in some circumstances\u2026Or maybe there were manipulated and misled by other Vampires plotting against Carna\u2026manipulated and misled into leaving her!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> After the PCs leave the Elysium, they are approached by the Nosferatu Vampire who informed them about the Carnian Vampire. He grins and asks how was it, and before the PCs can reply he goes on a tirade<br /> <i>\u201cSee, this is what happens when a 23 year old wiccan is embraced because her personal insights in her so-called book of shadows somehow impressed the esteemed Carna. Seriously, you know what she offered me in return for finding information about this potential lover? \u2018The Friendship of House Carna\u2019\u2026Looks to me like an empty promise with no guarantees in return for my efforts. I did not even bother to ask whether this would be a Minor or Major Boon because, seriously, Carnian Vampires? As far as I see it they are Tremere Vampires who bought into and got dazzled by the propaganda and outlook of a Vampire Elder cunningly establishing herself. More of the usual games within Clan Tremere, if you ask me.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> It is up to PCs to evaluate and consider who to believe. Maybe the Nosferatu has a point\u2026but it just might be true that the Friendship of House Carna is real and precious. It just might be true that there is much in loving magic for the sake of it and admitting the meaning and importance of the sacred <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">femininity. Of course, the benefits and value of the Friendship of House Carna might just depend on what Carna decides about it\u2026but that just might simply be the right way it works.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-24-2021, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T08:45:43-07:00","id":1464199,"title":"","content":"125)<br /> <br /> An independent Ghoul recently talked to a group of Kindred he met on the streets near the Rack. He behaved appropriately enough - after all, he has been doing it for over 15 years so far. Yet he made a slight mistake...he called himself a 'free Ghoul' while offering his services. Now, this wouldn't be so bad, except that there was this one particular Elder in this situation. Now, this Elder does not have anything against independent Ghouls, not at all. <i>However</i>, those of them who talk out loud about this, going so far as to say they are 'free Ghouls' (or using some other lofty term)...this is different.<br /> <br /> So it is that a hunt has been declared by the Vampire Elder. It might end up in tragedy, but it is thus that a point needs to be made..and some nightly entertainment has to be provided from time to time. Thus Ghouls - <i>loyal vassal Ghouls, unlike this particular fellow</i> - have been given details and directions about this so-called 'free Ghoul'. His car will be set on fire, and his apartment will likewise be firebombed (no worries, the fire likely won't spread around - the Ghouls have been informed to call the fire brigade on time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). He better get the hint to get out of the area quickly, cause soon after this it will be fair game in regard to eliminating him. Though fleeing will do him no good, as members and servants of the Camarilla all over the city have been informed to hound, harm, or kidnap him at the first opportunity. If he flees the city, the Elder's declaration will most likely follow him wherever he goes. After all, can he hide for long following over 15 years of getting his Vitae fix?<br /> <br /> Thus the only chance for the independent Ghoul is to carefully move around the city, staying in relatively safe public or well-hidden areas while hoping for the best. And actually, there is a way out for him. All he needs to do is to rethink his life choices, consider his situation, seek out a Kindred, apologize for his behavior, and offer his services to this one Kindred in particular, as a vassal Ghoul. Even if his service is not accepted, once the Elder gets informed about the attempt, he will deem that the point was made well enough and will call off the hunt, most probably... An experienced Ghoul can often be made useful again, after all. And his mistake wasn't <i>that </i>serious...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-22-2021, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T06:54:42-07:00","id":1464252,"title":"","content":"126)<br /> <br /> The vaunted Dominate Power of Oberon's Grail...just how useful can it be? And what exactly does forgetting an entire night do to a person's mind and life? A Tremere Elder intends to find out, and also to sharpen her skills with Dominate.<br /> <br /> A pair coming back from their first date? Intriguing. A businessman or a politician who just had an important meeting? Even better. A man just proposed to his future wife tonight? Perfect. A student returning from studying in the library for tomorrow's exam? Interesting, and he can still take the retake. Though rather than relying on chance meetings, the Elder found out that attending museums, exhibitions, and galas is the best way to single out suitable targets. The more a person might suffer or lose from being subjected to Oberon's Grail, the more interesting and intriguing it is. Obviously.<br /> She is sure to acquire some personal belongings or information (where they live or work) from the persons she targets, so that she can spy on them using Auspex or Thaumaturgy; to check up on the consequences of Oberon's Grail.<br /> <br /> The other Tremere in the city know about this, and they do have a strong suspicion that with how often the Elder is doing this, this could constitute a Masquerade violation...But none of them intend to inform anyone outside of the Clan, as House Tremere comes first. And fugue states and simple memory lapses do occur from time to time among mortals. Also, there might be plenty to learn and observe from the Elder's activities...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-24-2021, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:47:13-07:00","id":1464777,"title":"","content":"127)<br /> <br /> The mayor of the city has been trying to be too good for his own good. Did he really think his recent actions through? He gave a financial grant of 20,000 $ to a group aiding young writers, which is not bad in itself. However, he was clearly familiarized extensively and respectfully with details about a particularly reputable occult and esoteric store which hosts regular debates and lectures about culture, mysticism, history, and anthropology. And the details were described by a Tremere Ghoul working at the city hall, no less. Yet the mayor chose the dreary and formulaic prose of young writers. The Tremere Regent just won't have it. The esoteric store has an almost ideal location in one of the city's central areas, among its customers are some rich and noteworthy persons, and the blood bonded staff has proven capable enough in various tasks that Tremere Vampires set for them. The debates and lectures have been going good as well, and the Regent thinks that the place might be useful in recruiting mortals who might serve or be influenced by Clan Tremere.<br /> <br /> As such, the mayor has to go, despite his pretty good over five years tenure. Clearly, he is aversive to even the merest hint of the mystical and the occult. The Regent has some plans in regard to the city for the next months and years, and for the plans to succeed at least some of the important and influential mortals in the city need to be open and interested in regard to the mystical and intellectual ideals.<br /> <br /> Luckily, the city hall has been - with the Prince's agreement - under the influence and direction of the Tremere since the last nine years. As such replacing the mayor by the Tremere won't attract undue criticism or retaliatory actions from other Kindred. Most Vampires in the city will be informed about this coming change.<br /> It is unfortunate that the Prince has declared that the mayor, along with several other key mortals, cannot be blood bonded, Ghouled, or subjected to mental Disciplines.<br /> <br /> The question is thus how to arrange the mayor's downfall. The goal is to make him resign as soon as possible due to some scandal or ruining of his life.<br /> There is the option of arranging for a mistrial in an ongoing trial of several die-hard leaders of organized crime. And after this putting forwards a media campaign that will spin the criminals going free as a result of ties with the mayor. Certainly an idea.<br /> Pulling some strings and asking the politicians and businessmen who bribed the mayor for favors over the years to come forward? A fitting downfall, but might take relatively long.<br /> He has a wife (almost two decades of marriage) and a lover (since three years). If his lover would be blood bonded or subjected to Dominate and publically came out with the relation, would this be enough? Might just be what will be the easiest.<br /> <br /> Murdering is not an option because of the Regent's dislike of such crass methods, and a general unspoken rule in the Camarilla to avoid directly harming important mortals. Thus the Regent will have to carefully analyze and decide just how to ruin the mayor's life. And then he can start considering who might be the best next mayor - which would be the mayor who will benefit Clan Tremere the most, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-22-2021, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T06:55:14-07:00","id":1464869,"title":"","content":"128)<br /> <br /> A Ventrue Ancilla has been selected by the local Ventrue to establish amicable relation with at least some Gangrel Vampires in the city. One problem with this was that they barely attend Elysium or show up at usual places where Kindred meet and mingle. However, through careful observation and perseverance, the up-and-coming Ventrue managed to have a short conversation with a Gangrel, who turned out to be an Ancilla with a Domain on the outskirts of the city, near a small forest.<br /> <br /> After the initial exchange of pleasantries, the Gangrel Kindred turned out to be interested in cooperation in regard to seizing control of some of the city's administration. Apparently, city transportation is relatively clear (the Nosferatu have the metro, of course\u2026but that\u2019s it), and some money could be seized from various city renovation projects (including those involving green areas in the metropolis). The Gangrel would be trusted with watching and protecting the undertaking from intervention by other Vampires, and they could also perhaps contribute to the management and any plots of the seized assets (The Ventrue intended to have the lead in regard to this, of course).The Gangrel Vampire ended the conversation expressing his interest and asking for a Ghoul messenger with clear details and terms to meet him at particular spot on the edge of forest in his Domain. He promised to present the proposal from the Ventrue to his Clanmates.<br /> <br /> Thus the Ventrue Ancilla hammered out the details and the terms, and had his most trusted Ghoul memorize them. He also wrote them down in a notebook and gave it the Ghoul. The Ghoul has been instructed on some finer points of etiquette, and within the next few nights will meet the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> There is a slight problem, however. A Malkavian Neonate overheard almost the whole conversation between the Ventrue and the Gangrel while staying hidden, her Disciplines of Auspex and Obfuscate enabling her this. She walked in on the trusted Ghoul of the Ventrue and gave him an insidiously simple task with a Mesmerize \u2013 he is to carry an accessory to the meeting with the Gangrel, buying it on the way. The accessory \u2013 a shovel <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> Now, this is meant as a simple mockery \u2013 a reference to digging up Gangrel who use Earth Meld. Maybe it will sabotage the meeting and the chance of the Ventrue-Gangrel cooperation a bit\u2026or a lot\u2026this is the intention of the Malkavian. However, she does not know that this particular Gangrel Vampire was actually almost dug up during the day by Ghouls sent by an enemy. It ended up well \u2013 the Gangrel\u2019s Ghoul guardians (humans, not animals) realized they got distracted by some of the attackers away from his resting place, came back on time, and fought away the hostiles, killing two of them. Still, the danger was there, and the Gangrel Kindred likely will not react well to a Ghoul emissary carrying a shovel, while being unable to explain the fact.<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t have to end up in tragedy \u2013 it is not like the Ventrue Ghoul will try to attack or threaten the Gangrel with the shovel\u2026And he can still talk it out and lay out the proposal of Ventrue Vampires. But he just might leave with a few claw marks or broken bones, depending on the Gangrel\u2019s paranoia and mood.<br /> <br /> <br /> The PCs can encounter the Ghoul walking to the meeting with the shovel (or while the Ghoul will be buying the shovel), or somehow find out about the Malkavian\u2019s deed beforehand. Up to them as to what they will do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-25-2021, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T22:56:17-07:00","id":1465099,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:13px\">129)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Brujah Neonate wishes to put his Ghoul - one who he is almost certain in regard to the Embrace - through a trial. The man is largely noteworthy and interesting because he is a vehement intellectual, insisting that human societies and their idealogical ideas can be fully appreciated, understood, and influenced only when rigorous logic and careful analysis are applied. He has an air of confidence around him, but this is all in regard to high and serious matters. He lacks experience in the more simple, straightforward activities and achievements...like beating up a person till they bleed and their bones are broken.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">So the Neonate has come up with a plan - he will have the Ghoul take part in an underground cage fight, at a widely attended and popular place. His opponent will be one of the regulars, a simple brute selected in part for his appearance, as the Brujah knows his Ghoul for some reason dislikes men with stereotypical working-class features. The Ghoul's courage will be bolstered by the Brujah's Awe and encouragement. Thus he will most likely enter the fight without fear, despite lack of prior combat experience. After all, he is a loyal Ghoul who is aware of his greater strength and toughness, and also has quite the contempt for mundane humans.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Still, the Brujah will not risk the Ghoul losing the fight or being seriously harmed. His servant is important for him, and it would also damage the Vampire's reputation if his Ghoul would be defeated. As such, the opponent will be heavily drugged by a woman, who is a Malkavian Ghoul, offering him a drink laced with a sedative. Also, to encourage the Brujah's Ghoul to take it out on the defeated opponent, the audience will be incited to excitement and aggression by the Brujah Neonate and a few of his fellow Brujah. Thus the Ghoul might get some more direct, practical experience in matters he has never thought to involve himself in, like taking it out on a defeated opponent without fear or hesitation.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T10:27:24-07:00","id":1466489,"title":"","content":"130) A local elder tasks the coterie with dealing with a podcast, broadcast from their home city, which is about urban legends and conspiracies. This particular podcast apparently features a couple of men, and woman who is often exasperated by the verbal antics of the men. The podcasts is all about local conspiracies, and urban legends and lately has been getting too close to the truth. So much so it has alarmed some local vampire leadership (the Prince, the Primogen, random elder, etc.). The podcasters appear to be normal humans, and the podcast itself is recorded in a simple suburban home.<br /> <br /> The twist is the podcast is a trap set up by the S.I. They are exploring how aware the blankbodies are of social media and podcasts, and what will provoke a response. The podcasters themselves are each S.I. soldiers, have a lot of combat training and weapons at their disposal. There are also enough S.I. NPCs involved with the podcasters, as neighbors and the like, to make any attack on the podcasters quickly turn into a fire-fight nightmare, or even to capture any vampires making the effort.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T19:46:10-08:00","id":1469796,"title":"","content":"131) This plot hook occurred to me while watching the Christmas parade in my hometown.<br /> <br /> A Sabbat attack devastates a municipal Christmas parade, resulting in massive death and property damage in something the media calls a terrorist attack. (The PCs are on hand during the attack, for the sake of socializing, looking at the pretty lights, hoping for some discrete hunting or a combination of the above.) The scope of the attack overwhelms the party \u2013 they cannot play \u201cCaptain Vampire,\u201d neighborhood protector, and expect to survive.<br /> <br /> The coterie finds themselves caught up in the events and eventually discover the attack was a set up. Specifically, one elder in the city learned about the attack in advance but did not warn anyone because they sought to embarrass the vampire nominally responsible for organizing the parade. For example, in Chicago, Ballard might have learned about the attack but kept silent so as to embarrass Sovereign, who Prince Jackson had made responsible for the attack.<br /> <br /> The PCs are faced will make an enemy of the elder who permitted the attack if they reveal the truth to the local court, which will not punish the responsible elder in any case.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}